Subject: [PATCH] Present Tuna native password deltas without private keys

Source: https://download.gnome.org/sources/orca/50/orca-50.3.tar.xz
Source-SHA256: cc13521037519e06125ec6eb0236ffd52a6d6ff7ef538323f786fca840a3dbda

The native shell sets GLib prgname tuna-shell-gtk; its AT-SPI application
name is tuna-shell-gtk, not its org.tuna.Shell GApplication ID. Register
that exact app through Orca's normal Meson-installed GTK-subclass loader.

Own focused editable password insertion/deletion callbacks. Insertions
speak committed mask counts once, without payload/text reads or stale key
classification; deletion and system updates do not fabricate insertions.
Keep password key-echo and native braille updates. Classify only the first
matching post-edit caret through the actual version-specific event cache,
then delegate the complete GTK/default caret presentation handler.

Use the existing speak_character -> SSIPClient.char route. Orca initializes
that client with MESSAGE priority, which queues without interrupting itself;
no per-mask priority changes, artificial tokens or timing are required.

Preserve password text-change deltas through the 50.3 duplicate queue
filter, including equal-offset insert/delete/reinsert sequences. Preserve
focused password caret ordering before later navigation as well.

